    "result_text": "All green. The implementation is complete and the test suite passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0`). The audit log confirms the end-to-end behavior:\n\n```\nmemberId=NSWV22616E6609E9\n{\"schemaVersion\":2,\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"memberId\":\"NSWV22616E6609E9\",\n \"membershipLevel\":1,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Version 2, single source of truth** \u2014 new `util/IdentityVersion` holds `VERSION = 2` and `TAG = \"V2\"`, reused everywhere so `apiVersion`, audit `schemaVersion`, and the identifier tag can't drift apart.\n\n**The `V2` tag mixed *inside* each identifier** (so every value changes and no v1 value recurs):\n- `Postcodes.identityRegionCode(postcode)` = plain region + `V2` (`NSW`\u2192`NSWV2`); `AssignMemberId` now uses it, so the region *inside* the member id is tagged.\n- `HouseholdKey.id` now digests `\"V2|\" + key`.\n- `OwnerIdentity` now digests `\"V2|\" + telephone|email|soundex` (applies to both the stored key and duplicate detection, kept consistent).\n\n**User-facing fields stay plain** \u2014 I decoupled `locality`/`fiscalYear` from the member id: the mapper now derives `locality` straight from the postcode (`Postcodes.regionCode`, plain `NSW`) and `fiscalYear` from the registration date. `timezone` and `ownerSegment` build on that plain locality, so `V2` never leaks into them. The now-unused member-id parsers (`regionOf`/`fiscalYearLabel`) were removed rather than left to return wrong values for v2 ids \u2014 `MemberId` is back to a single responsibility (build/dedupe the id).\n\n**Response shape** \u2014 `openapi.yml` gains a nested `Identity` schema (`memberId`/`identityKey`/`householdId`), a top-level `apiVersion` integer, and drops the three top-level id fields; `OwnerMapper` assembles the `identity` object and stamps `apiVersion`.\n\n**Audit schema v2** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent` gains `schemaVersion: 2` and an `ownerSegment` recomputed from the version\u20112 identity's plain locality (`OwnerSegment.of(level, region)`).\n\nRequest fields are unchanged.",
