    "probe_text": "Read the whole pipeline (`owners.POST.yml` plus each function class). Here is exactly what happens, in order, for `POST /api/owners`. Every step runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the entire chain is one transaction committed at the end.\n\n## Precondition\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request is denied (403) before any step runs.\n\n## Steps in execution order\n\n1. **CheckIdempotencyKey** (entry) \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header and publishes it. If the key was already used *and* the original owner still exists, it republishes that owner and branches to **RespondWithOwner** \u2192 returns the existing owner with **200**, creating nothing. Otherwise it proceeds. *(side-effect: publishes key/replay owner)*\n\n2. **ValidateNewOwner** \u2014 binds the `@RequestBody` (the single read of the body) and rejects with `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (**400**) if any required field is missing/blank: `firstName`, `lastName`, address (either a non-blank structured `addressLine1` or a non-blank flat `address`), `city`, `telephone`. Publishes the validated request.\n\n3. **ValidateRegistrationDate** \u2014 if a `registrationDate` was supplied and it is after the server date \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**). Null is allowed.\n\n4. **ValidateOwnerPostcode** \u2014 if a postcode is present it must be a 4-digit value valid for the city's region \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**). Null/blank allowed.\n\n5. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** *(side-effect)* \u2014 normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` in place and sets `address` to the canonical form on the shared request.\n\n6. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** \u2014 converts telephone to E.164; if it can't form valid E.164 or the national-number length is wrong \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (**400**). *(side-effect: stores E.164 back on the request)*\n\n7. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** \u2014 if email present it must match the email regex \u2192 else `InvalidEmailException` (**400**). *(side-effect: stores trimmed, lower-cased email)*\n\n8. **ValidateEmailDomain** \u2014 if the (normalized) email's domain is on the disposable blocklist \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (**400**).\n\n9. **EnsureUniqueIdentity** \u2014 computes the derived identity key; if it exactly matches any non-soft-deleted existing owner's recomputed key \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**). (Single consolidated duplicate check.)\n\n10. **EnsureCityHasCapacity** \u2014 if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive, trimmed) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n11. **EnsureDailyLimit** \u2014 if \u2265 100 owners already registered on the request's effective business day \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` (**429**).\n\n12. **BuildOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps the request DTO to an `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`.\n\n13. **ResolveRegistrationDate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets the effective registration date (supplied, else today) rolled forward to a business day.\n\n14. **AssignMemberId** *(side-effect)* \u2014 computes the `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` member id (deduplicated against existing ids) and sets it.\n\n15. **AssignHouseholdId** *(side-effect)* \u2014 derives and sets `householdId` from last name + postcode.\n\n16. **AssignIdentityKey** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets the derived identity key on the entity (so it matches the duplicate-check key).\n\n17. **CountNamesakes** *(side-effect)* \u2014 counts pre-existing owners with the same first+last name and stores `namesakeCount`.\n\n18. **CountHouseholdMembers** *(side-effect)* \u2014 counts household members (starting at 1 to include the new owner) and stores `householdSize`.\n\n19. **CapMembershipLevel** *(side-effect)* \u2014 caps membership level at one above the highest among non-deleted household members; sets `membershipLevelCap` (no cap if household empty).\n\n20. **FlagBulkSignup** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if > 80 owners already registered on the day.\n\n21. **FlagCapacityWarning** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `capacityWarning = true` if the city holds between 40 and 49 owners (inclusive).\n\n22. **FlagPossibleDuplicate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` when a non-deleted owner shares the same last-name Soundex and postcode but a different identity key (skipped when `sharesHousehold` is true or postcode is blank).\n\n23. **SaveOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 persists the owner via `ownerRepository.save`.\n\n24. **RecordIdempotencyKey** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if a key was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in the idempotency store (so later replays return this owner).\n\n25. **AuditOwnerCreated** *(side-effect)* \u2014 emits two `AUDIT` log lines: a human-readable summary and a sequence-stamped structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON.\n\n26. **EnqueueWelcomeNotification** *(side-effect)* \u2014 emits a `NOTIFY` log line (owner id + member id) as the welcome hand-off.\n\n27. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** *(side-effect)* \u2014 responds **201 Created** with a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and the `OwnerDto` body.\n\n## Notes\n- **Validations** (fail the request): missing fields (400), future registration date (400), bad postcode (400), bad telephone (400), bad email syntax (400), disposable email domain (400), duplicate identity (409), city at capacity (409), daily limit (429). Order matters \u2014 e.g. field-presence is checked before format, and the guards run before the entity is built.\n- The escalation YAMLs under `officefloor/escalation/` map each of these exceptions to its HTTP status.\n- Everything from step 1 to 27 shares one transaction, so any thrown exception rolls back the whole create."
